Good! The warnings are normal (just line ending differences between Windows/Linux). But I notice you're adding some files you probably don't want in your repo:
Issues I See:

✅ .vscode/ folders - IDE settings (should be ignored)
✅ include/KHR/ and include/glad/ - These are external libraries (should be ignored)
✅ glad.c - External library source

You have 3 separate projects in subfolders: cmake_test_odev1, cmake_test_odev2, cmake_test_proje

Fix Before Committing:
Option 1: If these are all separate projects, make separate repos
Option 2: If this is one project with multiple assignments, clean it up:
1. Stop and create .gitignore NOW:
bash# Create .gitignore file
notepad .gitignore
```

**2. Add this to .gitignore:**
```
# IDE files
.vscode/
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user
*.suo

# Build artifacts
build/
bin/
obj/
out/
*.exe
*.dll
*.o
*.obj

# External libraries (GLAD is external)
**/include/KHR/
**/include/glad/
**/src/glad.c

# Or if you want to exclude specific folders:
cmake_test_odev1/include/KHR/
cmake_test_odev1/include/glad/
cmake_test_odev1/src/glad.c
cmake_test_odev2/include/KHR/
cmake_test_odev2/include/glad/
cmake_test_odev2/src/glad.c
cmake_test_proje/include/KHR/
cmake_test_proje/include/glad/
cmake_test_proje/src/glad.c